<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.alphalete.digi-docs-add</string>

    <!-- Install on LUCY 3 with:
             lucy rerun install_digi_docs_add_agent (add machine "Lucy 3")
         This pass adds people to OwnerVille, which SENDS THEM THE ONBOARDING
         EMAIL for the campaign they land on. It is a send.

         NOTE ON COMMENTS IN THIS FILE: never write two hyphens together
         inside an XML comment. It ends the comment early and makes the plist
         unparseable to plistlib even though plutil still accepts it, which
         shows up as a Hub card that cries wolf forever. The sibling
         blueink-docs-monday.plist has exactly that defect today. -->

    <!-- Path is the laptop placeholder; on Lucy 3, install_agent.py rewrites
         it to that machine's repo path. -->
    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/bin/bash</string>
        <string>/Users/megan/1st Claude Folder/deploy/digi_docs.sh</string>
        <string>--add</string>
    </array>

    <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
    <string>/Users/megan/1st Claude Folder</string>

    <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
    <dict>
        <key>PYTHONPATH</key>
        <string>/Users/megan/1st Claude Folder</string>
    </dict>

    <!-- 8:00am EVERY DAY, machine LOCAL time (Lucy 3 is Central). No Weekday
         key on purpose: this report fires on the date written above a chart,
         and those dates being Mondays is a coincidence of how the sheet gets
         filled in, not the rule (Megan 2026-08-26). A chart dated for a
         Wednesday has to be added on that Wednesday.

         Firing daily is cheap because the run stops on the sheet read when no
         chart is dated for today, long before it opens a browser. THE ADD PASS
         The document BUNDLE is the separate com.alphalete.digi-docs-send
         job, 30 minutes before each person's own start time. -->
    <!-- 10:30, moved from 11:00 (Megan 2026-09-14: "should we move this to
         10:30 to make sure it's good?"). 08:00 -> 11:00 happened on 2026-08-31
         because this hour is when the ONBOARDING EMAIL reaches every new
         start: a people-facing time, not a housekeeping one.

         WHY IT MOVED AGAIN. The pass now CREATES the OwnerVille records for
         anyone who has none, which is slower and more consequential than a
         plain campaign add — and it has to FINISH before the earliest bundle,
         which goes 30 minutes before that person's start. On 2026-09-14 the
         earliest start was 12:30, so 11:00 left one hour for a pass that took
         twenty minutes and had fifteen people to create. 10:30 doubles that
         margin and is still an hour anybody would call working hours.

         IT IS STILL NOT EARLY ENOUGH FOR EVERY COHORT. An 11:00 start needs
         its bundle at 10:30, the same minute this begins. Re-check against the
         tab's earliest Start Time whenever the cohort shifts earlier. -->
    <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
    <dict>
        <key>Hour</key>
        <integer>10</integer>
        <key>Minute</key>
        <integer>30</integer>
    </dict>

    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>/Users/megan/1st Claude Folder/output/logs/digi-docs-add.launchd.out.log</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>/Users/megan/1st Claude Folder/output/logs/digi-docs-add.launchd.err.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
